  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0109_415da2df31b5.png\" style=\"width: 277px; height: 250px;\" /></p><p>The slope of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; ( As,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;is perpendicular to the given line)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Mid-point of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;lies on the given line,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>Solving equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;we get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Which satisfy the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.</p>"
